PR #1157 — CodeRabbit Round-3 Feedback
Branch: fix/1156-fixed-asset-gaap-journals
Date: 2026-07-16

Summary of changes addressing all 5 actionable CodeRabbit round-3 comments.

---

1. accounting.utils.ts — validate accumulated depreciation ≤ acquisition cost
   File: apps/erp/app/modules/accounting/accounting.utils.ts (acquisitionLines)
   - Added a guard at the top of acquisitionLines() that throws
     "Accumulated depreciation cannot exceed the acquisition cost" when
     accumulatedDepreciation > acquisitionCost, before computing NBV or building
     any journal lines. A negative NBV would otherwise produce an absurd /
     unbalanced entry.
   - The only caller (postAssetRegistration in accounting.server.ts, run inside a
     Kysely transaction) is invoked from the register route inside try/catch, so
     the throw rolls the transaction back and surfaces the error to the user.
   - Added two unit tests: NBV=0 boundary (accum == cost) still balances; and the
     over-depreciated case throws.

2. register.tsx — companyId tenant scoping (2 queries)
   File: apps/erp/app/routes/x+/fixed-asset+/$fixedAssetId.register.tsx
   - Asset lookup (accounting-enabled path): added .eq("companyId", companyId).
   - Accounting-disabled status-flip update: added .eq("companyId", companyId).

3. register.tsx — handle zero-row update case
   File: same as #2, accounting-disabled update path.
   - Chained .select("id") after the .update() and now treat an empty result
     (zero rows matched — e.g. a concurrent update already moved the asset out of
     Draft) as a failure, redirecting with "Only Draft assets can be registered"
     instead of flashing a false success.

4. post-sales-invoice/index.ts — wrap asset record updates in the journal txn
   File: packages/database/supabase/functions/post-sales-invoice/index.ts
   - The two-step (ship-then-invoice) disposal path previously updated
     fixedAssetDisposal + fixedAsset via the supabase `client` during the
     array-building loop, BEFORE (and outside) the Kysely db.transaction() that
     posts the journals — so a journal-posting failure left the ledger and asset
     state inconsistent.
   - Deferred those two writes into a new `fixedAssetDisposalUpdates` array and
     apply them via `trx.updateTable(...)` inside the same db.transaction(),
     right before the salesInvoice status update. Kysely throws on error, so any
     failure now rolls back the posted journals. companyId scoping preserved.
   - Scope note: the direct/single-step disposal path (lines ~853-874) writes
     fixedAsset/fixedAssetDisposal via `client` too and has the same class of
     issue, but it was NOT flagged in the round-3 comments and falls outside the
     specified line range (710-726); left unchanged to keep the change focused.

5. tr/erp.po — physical inventory-count variance GL account translation
   File: packages/locale/locales/tr/erp.po (L5625-5626)
   - ALREADY CORRECT. The prior commit on this branch (df19d0de4,
     "fix(locale): correct and complete fixed-asset translations for #1157")
     had already realigned the scrambled GL-account tooltip block. The current
     msgstr —
       "Fiziksel sayım sonuçları sistemdeki stok miktarından farklı olduğunda
        etkilenen GL hesabı."
     — accurately renders msgid "GL account hit when physical counts differ from
     system inventory." The old (wrong) intercompany-debit string was already
     replaced. No change needed; no other locales touched.

